  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SAYULA LAGOON WATERSHED I</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Sayula Lagoon was one of the most important wetlands in the region for resting and feeding of migratory waterfowl and shorebirds, and has been recognized as an important wetland by national and international organizations. Before the construction, in 1989, of a road that crosses the lagoon, 1.3 million waterfowl were recorded in this region. This project will implement parts of the &apos;Sayula Lagoon Watershed Management Program,&apos; produced in part with prior NAWCA funding, by protecting 17,297 acres of wetlands through a management agreement, restoring 2,966 acres of seasonal wetlands, and rehabilitating two artificial wetlands. It will also include a community outreach</narrative>
  </description>
